[["heading","P RACTICAL PROJECT\nShopping cart logic"],["sinhala","","Jම් exercise එJකන් arrays, objects, functions, destructuring, spread, filter, map, reduce සහ",499],["sinhala","","validation එකට practice කරන්න පුළුවන්.",219],["heading","Task"],["text","Given a product list, select in-stock items, calculate the total, apply a percentage discount and\nreturn a new summary without changing the original list. Work in integer minor units for\nmoney."],["heading","Reference solution"],["code","const items = [\n  { name: \"Tea\", cents: 1000, qty: 2, stock: true },\n  { name: \"Milk\", cents: 500, qty: 1, stock: false },\n  { name: \"Rice\", cents: 2500, qty: 1, stock: true }\n];\nfunction summarize(items, discount = 0) {\n  if (!Number.isFinite(discount) || discount < 0 || discount > 100) {\n    throw new Error(\"Invalid discount\");\n  }\n  const available = items.filter(x => x.stock);\n  const lines = available.map(({ name, cents, qty }) => ({\n    name, total: cents * qty\n  }));\n  const subtotal = lines.reduce((s, x) => s + x.total, 0);\n  return { lines, subtotal,\n    total: Math.round(subtotal * (100 - discount) / 100) };\n}\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(summarize(items, 10)));"],["text","Expected subtotal: 4500 cents; total: 4050 cents. Tea: 2000, Rice: 2500."],["text","Interview question: Why use filter, map and reduce here?\nAnswer: filter selects available items, map converts them to line totals, and reduce\ncalculates the subtotal without mutating the input."],["heading","Extend it yourself"],["text","Group products by category with Map. Add validation for quantities and prices. Test zero\ndiscount, empty cart and invalid discount."],["heading","Next section"],["text","09. JavaScript in the Browser — DOM, events, asynchronous execution, APIs and browser\nstorage."]]